From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:29:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-snd: write TX buffers out without the BQL (tx-no-bql)

The TX thread (tx-poll-us) took the BQL for every pass, and the main
loop held the BQL for its device emulation, the GPU work of a video
among it. Measured on a Raspberry Pi 5 Xen DomD (2026-10-23, H.264
1080p60 in a WebView): the thread waited 15-66 ms for the BQL, the
ALSA output ran dry, and the guest's sound HAL reported missing data
hundreds of times in 10 minutes.

With tx-no-bql the thread writes each active stream's queued buffers
to the backend holding only the stream's queue_mutex, and moves the
buffers it has written out to a list of their own. Giving them back
needs the BQL (on Xen an interrupt raised without it is lost): the
thread does it itself when bql_trylock() succeeds, under the
transport's reentrancy guard as a bottom half would be, and leaves it
to a bottom half otherwise. The property needs tx-poll-us and an ALSA
audiodev with out.mixing-engine=off, out.try-poll=off and
out.fixed-settings=off, the case in which audio_be_write() goes
straight to snd_pcm_writei() with nothing shared with the main loop's
audio timer; realize refuses it otherwise. The main loop still drives
the PCM (START's prepare, a pending disable, the VM state handlers),
so START, STOP, PREPARE and close now run under queue_mutex, the
thread writes only while the stream is active and the VM runs (a VM
state handler at priority 1 tells it, ahead of the backend's drop and
after its prepare), and a voice opened again by PREPARE leaves the
stream inactive.

Measured the same way, 10 minutes a run (with the decoder-mode changes
of this series): the ALSA underruns qemu saw came to 0-3 a run, and
the sound buffers were given back within 17-26 ms in 99 cases of 100.
Off, the default, the device behaves as before apart from the locking
of START, STOP, PREPARE and close.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [this layer's virtio-snd TX thread (tx-poll-us)]
